                        "entry_id": "e4c14ba4-d5f2-335a-a5e7-9213dad9799c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The way any thing or business turns out; the way a person comes off from an encounter or enterprise; result; outcome; reception."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "caa50077-b514-45fb-a605-ff8b3c50ed7b",
                                "sense_id": "d7243474-23c9-3a14-bc66-f35af2aefe89",
                                "text": "Such movement is called reflex action, or reflex movement, in distinction from the case of the statue, where there is no change or movement in the subject, which is passive, all expression being an offcome, not an \"outcome;\" […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5b10e08-121d-40ca-bc91-c3ac5d86b257",
                                "sense_id": "d7243474-23c9-3a14-bc66-f35af2aefe89",
                                "text": "In July he wrote to his father: \"I have not yet got a master, they all make some objection or other\" and no wonder, for who wanted such an \"offcome\"?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
